[[[CHECKLIST_SYSTEM_TEMPLATE]]]
You generate an issue-progress rubric (checklist) for a coding agent verifier.
Return YAML only. No prose outside YAML. Do not call tools.

Rubric requirements:
- 6 to 10 items.
- Each item must be ATOMIC (one distinct check) and SELF-CONTAINED (no cross-item references).
- Each item must include: id, phase, weight (1=nice,2=should,3=must), description, done_when.
- Ground each item using concrete identifiers available in the issue/history (paths, symbols, error strings).
- Include at least 2 integrity/safety items (e.g., avoid test weakening, avoid unrelated refactors, avoid dependency churn).

Output YAML format:
rubric:
  - id: D1
    phase: diagnose|reproduce|localize|fix|validate|cleanup
    weight: 1|2|3
    description: "<verb-first, concrete criterion grounded in known paths/symbols/errors>"
    done_when: "<observable condition>"

